course: dictionary
lesson: 1652
title: Chinchillas and their thick fur
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A chinchilla is a small rodent from the Andes mountains of South America. It has very soft, thick grey fur and a bushy tail. «Chinchillas of the high Andes have one of the thickest furs of any land animal.» The word thickest tells you the fur is very dense, which keeps the animal warm in cold mountains.
explain: Read the words around chinchilla to find clues. «They bathe in dust because wet fur dries too slowly» tells you a chinchilla does not clean itself with water. The word dust and the word because both help you see that the dust is a special way to keep its fur clean and dry.
explain: Context also tells you about the animal's life. «Most pet chinchillas come from a few taken to the USA in the 1920s» shows that some people keep chinchillas as pets. Ask yourself: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: A chinchilla is a small rodent from the Andes mountains of South America.
fact: Chinchillas have one of the thickest furs on Earth, which helps them stay warm in the cold mountains.
fact: Chinchilla also means the fur of this animal, as in a coat made of chinchilla.
fact: Chinchillas clean their fur by rolling in dust, because wet fur dries too slowly.
fact: Both wild kinds of chinchilla are now endangered, after millions were hunted for fur coats in the 1800s and 1900s.
exercise: «Chinchillas of the high Andes have one of the thickest furs of any land animal.» Where do these chinchillas live? | In the Arctic ice | *In the high Andes mountains | In the deep ocean | In hot deserts in Africa
exercise: Which animal is a chinchilla? | A fish that lives in rivers | A bird that cannot fly | *A small rodent with very soft, thick grey fur and a bushy tail | A big spotted cat
exercise: «They bathe in dust because wet fur dries too slowly.» Why do chinchillas use dust? | Because they like the taste of dust | Because the dust is cold | *Because wet fur dries too slowly | Because dust makes them sneeze and sleep
test: «Millions of chinchillas were hunted for fur coats in the 1800s and 1900s.» What were chinchillas hunted for? | *Their fur | Their food | Their tails
test: «Porcupines carry thousands of barbed quills, chinchillas wear one of the thickest furs on Earth, and the tiny hazel dormouse curls into a tight golden ball to sleep.» Which animal wears one of the thickest furs on Earth? | Porcupine | Hazel dormouse | *Chinchilla
exam: «Most pet chinchillas come from a few taken to the USA in the 1920s.» What does a pet chinchilla most likely mean? | *A chinchilla that people keep at home | A chinchilla that lives wild in the Andes | A chinchilla that lives in the sea | A chinchilla made into a fur coat
